    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0100" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg16"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Storer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 26.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Rives’s No. 19, of the 18th ultimo, has
                    been received.</p>
                <p>The recognition accorded by the Austro-Hungarian Government to John Steel Twells
                    as “commercial (consular) agent” of the United States at Carlsbad is regarded by
                    the Department as sufficient.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
